.TH SECURITY 7 "August 2026" "toha3ee 0.1.0" "toha3ee"
.SH NAME
security \- responsible use, safety controls and scope
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B toha3ee
is an authorised-security console. Its modules can disrupt networks,
disconnect clients and capture credentials. Use it only on systems you own
or where you hold explicit written permission to test, and follow the scope
and rules of engagement you agreed.
.PP
toha3ee is intentionally
.B not
a malware or APT framework: it has no persistence, no command-and-control,
no anti-forensics and no EDR-evasion. Techniques that fall in that category
are deliberately excluded regardless of their defensive value.
.SH SAFETY CONTROLS
.TP
.B Preflight reports
Every module validates its environment and returns a report; blocked checks
must be cleared before
.B Run
is permitted.
.TP
.B Heartbeat watchdog
Long-running attacks must beat a watchdog; if they stall, the safety manager
flags them.
.TP
.B Automatic cleanup
Modules register cleanup hooks so stopping an attack restores the network to
its prior state (interface modes, forwarding, spoofed tables).
.TP
.B Risk classification
Each module carries a risk level (info, low, medium, high, critical) shown in
the catalogue.
.TP
.B Attack surface profile
.BR "net.profile"
ranks the vectors against the discovered target set before you run anything.
.SH BEFORE YOU TEST
.IP 1. 3
Get written authorisation naming the exact scope (hosts, subnets, time window).
.IP 2. 3
Test in an isolated lab you control before touching anything shared.
.IP 3. 3
Keep a snapshot of every VM so you can roll back a failed DHCP/WLAN test.
.IP 4. 3
Monitor your own traffic (Wireshark/tcpdump) so you know exactly what you emit.
.SH DISCLOSURE
If an engagement finds a real vulnerability, disclose it responsibly to the
owner and to any applicable vendor/cert process. Do not trade or sell the
findings.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR toha3ee (1),
.BR scripting (7),
.BR sudo (8)
.PP
The full policy lives in the repository: LICENSE, SECURITY.md,
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md and docs/security.md.
